3.2 on Sept 30th, 2026
- Bundled `elegantbook.cls` in the repository. It was missing, so a fresh clone could not build at all.
- Removed the unused `lastpage` package. It conflicted with `elegantbook` 4.7 (which disables
  hyperref's `pageanchor`) and produced a compile error.
- Fixed a typo in the source filename: `Introdution` → `Introduction`.
- Stopped tracking build artifacts (`*.bbl`, `*.synctex.gz`) and added `.gitignore`.
- Added `.latexmkrc`, so a bare `latexmk` builds with XeLaTeX and runs as many passes as needed.
- Rewrote the README.
- Minor grammar fixes: `a advanced` → `an advanced`, `a eye` → `an eye`,
  `2 ways` → `two ways`, `3 parts` → `three parts`.

3.1 on Jul 9th, 2026
- Migrated from `ctexart` to `elegantbook` document class. Removed 10+ redundant packages. Section levels shifted: `section`→`chapter`, `subsection`→`section`, `subsubsection`→`subsection`. Replaced custom title page with `\maketitle`.
- Removed page border, `tikz`, and `everypage` package.
- Replaced hand-rolled `mdquote` with ElegantBook's native `note`; added `warning`,
  `important`, `tip` via `\elegantnewtheorem`.
- Converted all `verbatim` + `adjustwidth` blocks to `\lstlisting[language=bash]`
  with GitHub-style rendering (rounded frame, light gray background, refined colors).
- All inline `\texttt` now have a light gray background.
- Changed `figure[H]` / `table[H]` to `[htbp]` for better float placement.
- Fixed Preface and Afterwards chapter headers (missing `\chaptermark`).
- Cleaned up duplicate font preamble.

3.0 on Jul 9th, 2026
- Migrated the tutorial from Debian 12 to Fedora 44: replaced `apt` with `dnf`, `.deb` with `.rpm`, updated all distro references.
- Rewrote Part 2 (Advanced Usage) and Part 3 (Dual OS), including new sections on anti-cheat, Nvidia drivers, and software recommendations.
- Fixed TOC hyperlink for Preface and Afterwards (missing `\phantomsection`).

2.1 on Mar 1st, 2025
- Added a new section `File Descriptor and Redirection Operators` in `Some trivial contents on Linux`.
- Added a new section `VSCode LaTeX Environment` in `Decorate your own garden`.
- Changed `rm` to a safer action in `Linux file commands`.
- Added a new chapter `Having heard Dao in the morning` in `Advanced Usage`.

2.0 on Feb 26th, 2025
- The first formal release of the project on GitHub.